## 3. Evidence plan

Each obligation names what is produced, how it is verified, and — per `CANARY-0002` — what makes
it **discriminating**: a check that returns the same result whether the claim or its negation
holds is vacuous, however faithfully it reproduces (`constitution/canaries/CANARY-0002.json`).

| id | unit | evidence | kind | verification | discriminating because |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| E-0.1 | W0.1 | resolved path of §4.3 + the parsed node-type list | DETERMINISTIC | `rg -n '4\.3' <schema_source>` returns the node-type section | a wrong/absent path yields no node types → R-3 fires, so the check separates "schema readable" from "schema assumed" |
| E-0.2 | W0.2 | enumeration of sealed goals with kinds | DETERMINISTIC | corpus listing filtered to `state == SEALED`, grouped by `goal_kind` | if <3 sealed or all one kind, the listing shows it → `S-INVALID`; a fabricated corpus fails path resolution in E-6 |
| E-0.3 | W0.3 | write probe on `reviews/spikes/` | DETERMINISTIC | a create+delete of a scratch file in the target dir | a denied write is observable, not inferred |
| E-0.4 | W0.4 | verbatim §9/A8 quote + locator, or "no threshold stated" | ATTESTED (quote) | quote must match the source at the cited locator | forces R-3 to be *found* rather than argued around; an invented threshold has no locator |
| E-1 | W1 | `ProbeConfig` with `frozen_at`, published pre-W2 | DETERMINISTIC | frontmatter of the report reproduces the frozen values byte-for-byte | any post-hoc tuning shows as a mismatch between the published config and the one used in W7 |
| E-2 | W2 | `Goal[3]` records: id, kind, sealed_at, artifact paths | DETERMINISTIC | re-running the selection rule (sealed filter → stratify → lexicographic tiebreak) reproduces the same 3 ids | a deterministic rule makes cherry-picking visible: a different set means the rule was not followed |
| E-3 | W3 | `NodeTypeSchema[]` + computed `denominator` | DETERMINISTIC | `denominator == 3 × Σ_nodetypes |required fields|`, recomputed from the parsed schema | a hand-authored denominator won't match the parse — this is the arithmetic that makes `loss_ratio` meaningful |
| E-4 | W4 | seeded row count | DETERMINISTIC | row count in the report == cross-product size from E-3 | catches silently skipped fields (I-2), the single highest-yield route from NO-GO to GO |
| E-5 | W5.* | per-field table: verdict + citation + note | ATTESTED (hand extraction) | rubric §5.1 applied; each row independently re-judgeable from its citation | the citation lets a reviewer re-run the judgement call; without it, `extractable` is unfalsifiable |
| E-6 | W6 | audit report: I-1 + I-2 + citation resolution | DETERMINISTIC | every non-`absent` row has a citation **and** the cited path exists; row count matches | this is the check that separates a real report from a fabricated one — the G-2 gap the shape-only accept checks leave open |
| E-7 | W7 | `loss_ratio` + raw totals `{extractable, partial, absent, denominator}` | DETERMINISTIC | recompute `(absent + 0.5 × partial)/denominator` from the published table | anyone can re-derive it; the ratio cannot drift from the table |
| E-8 | W8 | R-1/R-2/R-3 evaluation, including non-firing rules | DETERMINISTIC | per-node-type rollup shown explicitly in the `## aggregate` section | R-2 is invisible in the aggregate ratio; showing the rollup is what makes it checkable |
| E-9 | W9 | the deliverable + accept-check transcript | DETERMINISTIC | the four commands in §5, run and their output recorded | shape-only (see §5 caveat) — E-6 carries the substantive weight |
| E-10 | W10 | escalation record + recommended regex | ATTESTED | acknowledgement from the accept-criteria owner | — |

**Anti-forgery discipline (CANARY-0001).** `constitution/canaries/CANARY-0001.json` defines forged
evidence as a claimed result its `reproducible_command` does not produce; the detection signature
is a kernel re-run yielding a different result. Applied here: E-1, E-3, E-4, E-6, E-7 are all
*recomputations* from published inputs. Every number in the report must survive re-derivation by a
reader who did not run the probe.

**Anti-vacuity discipline (CANARY-0002).** The design's G-2 stands: the four accept checks verify
shape only — a report with 3 fabricated goals and `loss_ratio: 0.1` passes all four. E-6 is the
mitigation, and it is a **required** obligation, not an optional strengthening: it is the only
evidence in this plan that references the artifacts under review rather than the report's own
formatting.

