## 5. Acceptance mapping

| accept check | satisfied by | caveat |
|---|---|---|
| `test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md` | W9 (requires W0.3) | — |
| `rg -q '^verdict: (GO\|NO-GO)$' …` | W8 → W9 frontmatter | token must be at column 0, exactly `GO`/`NO-GO` |
| `test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' …) -ge 3` | W2 → W9 goal sections | heading form `## goal: <id>` exactly |
| `rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' …` | W7 → W9 frontmatter | **cannot match `1.0`** — G-1, see W10 |

All four are *shape* checks (design G-2). The plan's substantive acceptance is **E-6**: every
non-`absent` row carries a citation that resolves. Recommend the gate adopt E-6 as a fifth check.

